form. Wish more places did it. After a liter and a half of great beer we finis..."},{"business_id":"MqFQqNhMRaizyVRwsea6EA","review_id":"_s9qN8gJQu-Yhbk8wx18jg","date":"2017-09-17T18:08:11","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9445526599884033,"text_excerpt":"This place is so freaking cool, y'all! It really reminded me of being at the biergartens in Munich. We sampled a little of everything: the Berliner sandwich, the pork schnitzel plate with potato dumplings, and a cheese pretzel with beer cheese for dipping. Every single thing was off the chain! The beer cheese is just as good as other yelpers have said, but the pretzel was so cheesy it didn't even need it. The Berliner comes with a curry ketchup that I wish I could purchase in 5-gallon increments, and the schnitzel and dumplings were identical to the authentic ones I've had before. Also tried the beer, which comes in 1/2 liter or full liter glasses, so you're good whether you want to take ..."},{"business_id":"MqFQqNhMRaizyVRwsea6EA","review_id":"S1pZSHtpet-gbIQNh7Ql8g","date":"2019-02-12T22:30:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9440096616744995,"text_excerpt":"This is a cool little place in the Bywater. I went with my husband and our two young boys for lunch, and we really enjoyed our food and the overall friendly and quaint ambience. I love when places are kid-friendly. They have a kids section on the menu with good selections. I really enjoyed my Nuremburger! It had the most delicious sauerkraut I've ever had. I never imagined sauerkraut could taste so good! I think my husband had a plate called the Berlin, and it had these very crispy, tasty little onions and this savory and sweet sauce, that was fantastic. I only wish they had included fries. The waitress was so pleasant. We are also tried their \"king cake\". The filling in the pretzel is ve..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"MqFQqNhMRaizyVRwsea6EA","photo_id":"KlLQvG7HGieDe4GcRgjlpg","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/KlLQvG7HGieDe4GcRgjlpg.jpg",